<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22611" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-cresco</span></b> , ēvi, v.
		n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to grow
				in</i> or <i>upon</i> any thing (perh. not
			ante-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non taedia animalium capillis increscunt,</span>”
				<i>do not grow in the hair</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					28, 11, 46, § 163</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In
			gen., <i>to grow</i>, <i>increase</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lacrimis quoque flumina dicunt Increvisse suis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					11, 48</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">maxime cibo eget, qui increscit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 1,
					3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ne cum increverint (arbores),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col. 3,
					21</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>To grow</i> or <i>increase in</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animis discordibus irae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 9, 688</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In
			gen., <i>to increase</i>, <i>augment</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">morbus increscit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 3,
					2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dolor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Med. 951</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">audacia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					1, 33, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">certamen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					10, 5, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fremitus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					45, 1, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">increscere et invalescere sententiam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					33, 7, 12</span></i>
			.— Rhet., <i>to advance from weaker to
				stronger expressions</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hoc genus increscit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint.
					8, 4, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
